# Charter Fishing Tampa Bay

> Private fishing charters on Tampa Bay, Florida, run by a crew of four local captains: Capt. William Ashmore, Capt. David Pruner, Capt. Frankie Gonzalez and Capt. Rob Hahn. Inshore, nearshore, offshore (deep sea) and freshwater crappie trips. Prices are per boat, from $550. 133 five star Google reviews. Call or text {{ site.phone }}.

Key facts:

- Service area: Tampa Bay from Ruskin to St. Petersburg, the Gulf of Mexico past the mouth of the bay, and the Kissimmee area lakes (Lake Kissimmee, Lake Toho, Crooked Lake) for crappie.
- Trip lengths: 4, 6 or 8 hours. Morning trips leave at 8:00 AM; most 4 and 6 hour trips can also leave at 1:00 PM.
- Included: captain, rods, reels, tackle, bait and saltwater fishing licenses. Crappie anglers bring a Florida freshwater fishing license.
- Booking: a 10% deposit holds the date; if the weather is unsafe, guests get a new date or the deposit back.
- Book online: {{ site.booking }}

